note: design 54.4: edits with the same pattern are one line of the gap list, with the count of the places. The line with the most places comes first.
note: a line with two places and a pattern that holds proposes `--same`. A line with one place proposes `--change`. A short list has no line "and N more". Design 84: a body line has "MIR changes" (not decided), so it has the two forms; `far` (no checked configuration compiles it, with a reason) has no result and keeps the plain form and the command.
option: --reason
option: depot::far=a function of the windows build only
rule+: R54.4-2 R54.4-3
rule-: R54.4-2 R54.4-3 R54.4-4 R54.4-7
exit: 0
must_match: (?s)2 site\(s\): changed expression `c\.total` → `c\.total\(\)`[^\n]*\n      not stated \([^\n]*\(one statement for 2 places: f\d\)\n
must_match: \n      not stated \([^\n]*\); to state it: the check did not decide if the behavior changes: if it changes, --change 'depot::a,depot::b=TEXT'; if it does not change, --same 'rewrite \$a\.total => \$a\.total\(\)'
must_match: changed literal `10` → `11` [^\n]*\n      not stated \([^\n]*\); to state it: the check did not decide if the behavior changes: if it changes, --change 'depot::limit=TEXT'; if it does not change, --same 'rewrite 10 => 11'
must_match: changed literal `1` → `2` [^\n]*\n      not stated \([^\n]*\); to state it: --change 'depot::far=TEXT'\n
must_not_match: one statement for 3 places
must_not_match: \n      not stated \([^\n]*\); to state it: --change 'depot::a=TEXT'
must_not_match: more line\(s\)
must_match: \n  to state them, add facts to the stored step \(no build check runs again\): semilla fact --step 0 
must_not_match: add these options to the command of the step
